<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Fabricator.Bridge</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Fabricator.Abstractions</AssemblyName>
    <Description>
      The stable, minimal contract surface for the fabricator bridge: the provider/function interfaces and the
      Arrow-typed POCOs that cross the host&lt;-&gt;provider/plugin boundary. Kept in the Fabricator.Bridge namespace
      (assembly split only — no source churn). Plugins reference THIS + Apache.Arrow (host-provided); it carries
      no ABI/marshaling internals. Shared (default-context) assembly — the prerequisite for AssemblyLoadContext
      plugin isolation. See docs/plugin-system.md.

      The layering, one-way and enforced by the reference graph being acyclic:
        Fabricator.Abstractions   contracts + the service registry   (Apache.Arrow only)   &lt;- required
        Fabricator.Common         reusable implementations                                 &lt;- optional
        Fabricator.Bridge         ABI, host, Azure/Fabric, unsafe                          &lt;- never, for a plugin
      A type here must be CONTRACT. An implementation belongs in Common; anything needing the running host is
      a SERVICE (FabricatorServices). docs/plugin-services.md sections 7.2 and 9.
    </Description>

    <!-- PACKABLE. Directory.Build.props turns packing OFF for the whole folder; these two assemblies are the
         only ones a plugin may reference, so they are the only ones that opt back in.
         /!\ PackageId is UNRESERVED on nuget.org: `Fabricator.Abstractions` is free but the bare `Fabricator`
         ID is TAKEN by an unrelated package (checked 2026-09-02), so a `Fabricator.*` prefix reservation is
         unlikely to be granted. That binds nothing while packages go to a local folder or a release asset;
         revisit the ID before publishing to nuget.org. docs/plugin-services.md section 5 Q4. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Fabricator.Abstractions</PackageId>
    <PackageDescription>The stable contract surface a fabricator PLUGIN compiles against: the provider and function interfaces, the Arrow-typed POCOs that cross the host boundary, and the host-service locator. Reference this and Apache.Arrow; nothing else is required to write a plugin.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageTags>duckdb;fabricator;plugin;arrow</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Apache.Arrow" Version="23.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
